e},{"text":"Implementation matches AC","done":true},{"text":"Solution fits project architecture","done":true},{"text":"Tests green","done":true},{"text":"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted","done":true},{"text":"If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches","done":true},{"text":"Scoped closed-shape validation exists for Sections 10.1-10.4 and is invoked on the composed production path before identity is calculated or verified: exact top-level and nested member sets, and BlobChunk index/offset/size order, bounds and coverage invariants, with the composed call site named in evidence","done":true},{"text":"Negative tests and fuzz corpus cover an unknown top-level member, an unknown nested member, invalid chunk bounds/order/coverage, and closed Transfer Manifest nested shapes; each must make identity calculation and verification refuse rather than attest","done":true},{"text":"tracecheck -section 17.3 passes for the implemented identity contribution without claiming migration publication or atomic-reference behavior that README correctly reports unavailable","done":true},{"text":"AUDIT, not spot-fix: every open or extension point in closed_shapes.go validates its full key grammar per Section 1.6, and every string[n..m] bound counts Unicode characters rather than UTF-8 bytes; both directions are proven, an invalid key of any namespace is refused and a valid multibyte value at the character bound is accepted","done":false},{"text":"Every fuzz target the candidate defines is invoked by the configured validation suite with a fixed -fuzztime, including the closed-shape target; a newly added target that is not wired into the suite is a gate gap","done":false}]
